<title>UK: Psion up further after Hoare Govett &quot;buy&quot;.</title>
<headline>Psion up further after Hoare Govett &quot;buy&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Psion Plc rose on Monday, extending Friday's sharp rise sparked by a &quot;buy&quot; recommendation from analysts at ABN AMRO Hoare Govett, dealers said.</p>
<p>Shares in the maker of handheld computers were up 9p at 412-1/2 by 1215 GMT in thin volume of 58,075 shares, after leaping on Friday by 36-1/2p.</p>
<p>Analyst Judith Allen at Hoare Govett said she had repeated a buy on Psion because of its strong position in the handheld computer market, which gave the company scope to expand into related markets.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
